# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nivavale — environment variables (example)
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development:
#       copy .env.example .env.local
# 2. Fill in real values.
# 3. Never commit `.env.local` or any real secrets to the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Contact form endpoint (optional override).
#
# Leave this unset: the form posts to /api/contact, the Cloudflare Pages
# Function in functions/api/contact.ts, which emails submissions to
# info@nivavale.com. Set it only to use an external form service instead
# (Formspree, Basin, and so on).
#
# NOTE: this value is inlined into the public JavaScript bundle at build time,
# so it must never contain an API key or any other secret.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_ENDPOINT="https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id"
#
# The email provider's own secrets (RESEND_API_KEY, CONTACT_TO, CONTACT_FROM)
# are server-side only. They are configured in the Cloudflare dashboard and,
# for local development, in .dev.vars — see .dev.vars.example.
